WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.890
- [Woman] Social media has
become part of our nature.

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.210
We post, we share, we like,

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.993
we follow, we unfollow, we subscribe.

00:00:08.271 --> 00:00:10.623
But how is social media affecting us?

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:14.350
A small study of 20 college
students found a correlation

00:00:14.350 --> 00:00:16.410
between students who
demonstrated higher levels

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.160
of Facebook addiction in activity

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.760
of the amygdala striatal
system while they interacted

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:21.903
with Facebook signals.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.000
This activation was
the same scene in those

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.250
with substance addiction.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:31.363
In a 2016 UCLA study, teens
were split into two groups.

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.090
One were shown a photo with
a high number of likes,

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:36.100
and the other group was
shown the same photo

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:37.300
but with fewer likes.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.340
Those who viewed the
photo with more likes,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:41.510
were more likely to like
the photo themselves

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:44.010
than the group who saw the
photo with fewer likes.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.383
Again, it was the same picture.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.030
This experiment found
activity in multiple parts

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:50.580
of the brain when teens saw photos

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:52.840
they took receive a lot of likes.

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.450
In particular, this study
found significant activity

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.260
in part of the brain's reward circuitry

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.043
known as the nucleus accumbens.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.380
Dopamine is released in
the brain after positive

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:03.390
social stimuli, such as likes

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.393
and positive comments on social media.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:11.420
That photo she just posted,
she got a bunch of likes,

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:13.060
releasing dopamine into her brain

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:15.013
and causing a feeling of satisfaction.

00:01:15.076 --> 00:01:17.743
(loud applause)

00:01:18.113 --> 00:01:21.113
(loud upbeat music)

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.800
Psychologist B.F. Skinner
found that mice would respond

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.410
to certain stimuli they
knew resulted in a reward

00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:38.723
more often when the reward
came at variable times.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:41.050
This theory can also be
applied to social media

00:01:41.050 --> 00:01:43.170
and the times we check
it looking for a reward

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.673
in terms of a like, comment, or message.

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:47.520
We habitually check our accounts,

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.163
but we are not always rewarded.

00:01:49.347 --> 00:01:52.297
Maybe this photo didn't get
the amount of likes you wanted.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.940
So you will try again and again and again

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:56.363
looking for that reward.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.223
But wait, something else.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:01.380
Have you ever felt your phone vibrate

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:02.430
when it really didn't?

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:04.000
According to Robert Rosenberger

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.013
of the Georgia Institute of Technology,

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.030
we've become so connected to our phones,

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.380
that they've sort of
become part of our bodies.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.950
Any time something stimulates
and triggers sensation

00:02:12.950 --> 00:02:14.762
in any area where you keep your phone,

00:02:14.762 --> 00:02:16.320
you might believe it's your phone.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.420
This is called phantom vibration syndrome.

00:02:18.420 --> 00:02:20.620
Studies show that nearly 90% of people

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:22.953
report experiencing
these phantom vibrations.

00:02:23.475 --> 00:02:26.058
(machine hums)

00:02:26.854 --> 00:02:30.604
(playful instrumental music)

